Besides starting with default profiling information record (discussed in flightrecording), there are roughly 3 
approaches to perf debugging using JRMC:

[a] Profile: Thats right, start jrmc, click on the JVM and start flight recording.

[b] Lock Profile: Same as above but click on lock profile and make sure the JVM is started with the correct option

[c] Memleak: Monitor Growth Rate of classes. Find the reddest one, click "add to type graph" and keep expanding until
    you reach the outermost class whose objects are keeping these class objects alive.

    Now click on get instances, find the highest few objects, click on add to type graph then click to get to Root.
    
    That should give you the Dominator object possibly responsible for the leak.
    http://www.javabeat.net/2011/09/the-memory-leak-detector-oracle-jrockit/

